      ratio      = fraction of the chunk's variation surviving conditioning on obs
      floor(hi)  = (pi/2)*mean_cell(sigma_cell) straight from the k neighbours --
                   an UPPER bound: a neighbour is not at zero observation distance,
                   so real obs-driven variation leaks into the estimate
      floor      = the same quantity extrapolated to zero obs distance.
                   Still an UPPER bound on the flow objective (see the docstring):
                   it prices each of the 350 chunk cells independently, while the
                   flow head sees x_tau for ALL of them and this ambiguity is one
                   scalar -- `when does the lift start` -- so it aggregates 350
                   noisy readings of a single latent. Expect the training mse to
                   land BELOW this and above zero.
